These passing assertions reproduce the mismatch; they are **not** evidence that the behavior has been fixed. An earlier test-fixture attempt omitted the required tool-result `isError` field and failed before reaching capture for that case; it is not counted as an OpenClaw failure.

### Source / ordering evidence

Pinned to `v2026.10.2`:

- [`attempt-prompt-phase.ts`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/v2026.10.2/src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-prompt-phase.ts#L221): the runner awaits `before_agent_run` before prompt submission.
- [`attempt-llm-boundary.ts`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/v2026.10.2/src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-llm-boundary.ts#L363): `installModelPromptProjection` captures later inside `agent.transformContext`.
- [`user-turn-transcript-updates.ts`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/v2026.10.2/src/sessions/user-turn-transcript-updates.ts#L52): capture rewrites the current original, then publishes the updated receipt.
- [`user-turn-transcript.ts`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/v2026.10.2/src/sessions/user-turn-transcript.ts#L355): `refreshAdmission` updates the recorder; it does not rerun the original admission handler as a post-projection plugin gate.

The inspected public `before_agent_run` and CE `assemble` contracts do not expose the active recorder for this purpose. `llm_input` / `model_call_started` are observational, not awaited fail-closed dispatch boundaries. The custom CE already uses `systemPromptAddition`, and its own prompt hook uses `appendSystemContext`, so moving its own text out of `prependContext` is not a repair here.

### Impact and severity

Confirmed on one custom durable CE integration: background-completion processing and durable turn advancement can remain blocked after otherwise valid admission. The host-level projection mismatch reproduced in both synthetic history sizes. Frequency across other plugins/providers is **NOT_ENOUGH_INFO**. No data loss or unauthorized disclosure is asserted.

