Talk transcription using `elevenlabs/scribe-v2` through OpenRouter includes background-sound annotations such as “jingle” and “outro jingle.” OpenRouter supports disabling these with `provider.options.elevenlabs.tag_audio_events: false`, but OpenClaw’s OpenRouter STT adapter does not forward that option.

For example, this configuration is accepted but cannot disable audio-event tagging:

```json
{
  "tools": {
    "media": {
      "models": [
        {
          "provider": "openrouter",
          "model": "elevenlabs/scribe-v2",
          "capabilities": ["audio"],
          "providerOptions": {
            "openrouter": {
              "tag_audio_events": false
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "audio": {
        "enabled": true
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The same option can be configured under `tools.media.audio.providerOptions.openrouter`. Options under `providerOptions.elevenlabs` do not reach the OpenRouter adapter.

The media runner merges provider options into `params.query`, but the [OpenRouter adapter](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/extensions/openrouter/media-understanding-provider.ts) only reads `temperature`. Its outgoing transcription body contains `model`, `input_audio`, and optional `language` and `temperature`; the configured audio-event option is omitted.

Expected: provide a documented mapping to [OpenRouter’s supported transcription options](https://openrouter.ai/blog/announcements/elevenlabs-on-openrouter/). For this configuration, the request should include:

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "options": {
      "elevenlabs": {
        "tag_audio_events": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

There is an open design point: OpenClaw’s config schema only accepts flat provider-option values. The adapter could derive the OpenRouter options slug from the model prefix (`elevenlabs/scribe-v2` → `elevenlabs`). That works for Scribe, but options can be silently dropped when another provider serves the model. Would maintainers prefer allowing nested objects in `providerOptions`, so users can specify the OpenRouter provider namespace explicitly?

Please preserve explicit boolean `false`, model-entry precedence over audio defaults, and existing requests when options are absent. Document the supported configuration and cover the outgoing request body with a regression test.

Related: [#168580](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/168580) and [#177975](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/177975) address direct ElevenLabs transcription, not the OpenRouter adapter.

