### Additional information

#### Source explanation

- [src/channels/inbound-event/session-transcript-context.runtime.ts:62-82](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/489774034984cd3ef78706125f20f4b25723288b/src/channels/inbound-event/session-transcript-context.runtime.ts#L62-L82) counts ID-bearing history candidates and requests `limit: candidates * 2`.
- [src/config/sessions/transcript-recent-text.ts:60-135](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/489774034984cd3ef78706125f20f4b25723288b/src/config/sessions/transcript-recent-text.ts#L60-L135) admits qualifying user/assistant text without requiring an external transport message ID. The internal input and `NO_REPLY` therefore consume entries too.
- [src/config/sessions/transcript-recent-text.ts:138-172](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/489774034984cd3ef78706125f20f4b25723288b/src/config/sessions/transcript-recent-text.ts#L138-L172) stops after the requested number of projected text entries, not after enough external candidates or logical turns have been covered.
- [extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.recent-history.ts:40-85](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/489774034984cd3ef78706125f20f4b25723288b/extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.recent-history.ts#L40-L85) budgets physical platform rows before exclusions. [extensions/discord/src/monitor/provider.ts:183-186](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/489774034984cd3ef78706125f20f4b25723288b/extensions/discord/src/monitor/provider.ts#L183-L186) supplies the default 20-row Discord limit.

The source explicitly describes the heuristic as approximate:

> Roughly one user row and one reply per answered turn; a shorter read only keeps rows.

Thus retention on missing evidence is intentional and safer than dropping unproven input. The defect is insufficient coverage of still-selected candidates, not incorrect fail-open behavior. Raising the ratio happens to fix this fixture but is not established as a general repair; merely filtering `NO_REPLY` is likewise not proven sufficient.

#### Repair acceptance criteria

- Cover the six-candidate fixture with and without internal runtime pairs and demonstrate that internal activity alone does not resurface the answered target.
- Use bounded candidate-aware coverage or another justified owner-level approach; no unbounded scan is requested.
- Preserve exact ID/body matching, attachment caution, incomplete-answer retention, active-session and agent scope, and conservative retention when evidence really is unavailable.
- Verify both the transcript reader/reconciliation boundary and the next rendered native input. Test candidate count independently of platform-row count.

#### Status and evidence limits

The omission owner and private transcript projector match upstream `main` at `6c32a15729f269d6ed44b89713eb6ae004f15ab1`. The fresh reproduction uses exact production code with synthetic reader output, not a new real Gateway/SQLite/channel experiment. The historical reconstruction and native-input observation are separate evidence.

This is a demonstrated limitation of the existing conservative heuristic, not a bisected regression or a missing-final-answer report. No product, configuration or stored transcript was modified.

