### Production context

On 2026.10.10 this path was reached repeatedly. Five scheduler outages between 2026-11-06 and 2026-11-11 each started with `agent database clean-close receipt: close-unconfirmed`. The cancelling caller was an agent polling its own finished background exec while that exec's completion event was reopening the agent's database. A backport of this change kept the Worker for every such refusal (three on 2026-11-12 alone). That evidence is from 2026.10.10, not from this branch.

Closes https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/197824

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: a Discord slash command reply loses all of its text when one of its attachments fails to load (a remote URL that answers 404, or a local file outside the allowed media roots).

## User Impact

User impact: the slash command answer still arrives, with a receipt line such as `⚠️ missing.png: Delivery failed. Try sending this file again.` for each file that could not be attached; attachments that loaded are still sent.

## Why This Change Was Made

Discord's interaction reply delivery loaded every attachment in one step before the first follow-up, so one `MediaFetchError` or `LocalMediaAccessError` aborted the whole reply. Agent, plugin command and `/status` replies all go through this one delivery function. It now catches those two load errors per attachment and appends the existing receipt from `appendReplyMediaFailures`, matching the Telegram fix in https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/186751 (same error types, same receipt and label). Other errors still throw.

The change is limited to `extensions/discord/src/monitor/native-command-reply.ts`. Unlike Telegram, which loses all media of the reply in that fallback, Discord loads each file separately here, so it keeps the files that loaded and receipts only the ones that failed.

A failed attachment is logged at verbose level only (the URL or path and the load error, no message content): this delivery function has no runtime logger at hand, its one log call is the same `logVerbose` it uses when an interaction expired, and the receipt line already shows the failure in the reply.

## Evidence

Tested at `f2974fbb491` (base `main` `5d6a026e4375`).

What ran for real: the Discord plugin's slash-command entry points (an agent reply through the channel turn pipeline, and a registered plugin command), the reply delivery, and media loading against a real public URL that answers HTTP 404. Stand-ins: the model turn was replaced by one fixed final reply, Discord's interaction API (`reply` / `followUp`) was recorded instead of called, and for the plugin command the route resolution and the session-store read were stubbed. The real media loader was wrapped only to record the load error behind each receipt. The same harness (internal names removed) is in the details block below; it ran on the base and on this branch, each run stamped with its commit.

